{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"Under Rule 6c-11, an AP must be a participant of an SEC-registered clearing agency, **or have an arrangement with such a participant** to effect the ETF share transactions through that agency. It must also have a written agreement allowing it to place creation/redemption orders. That agreement may be with the ETF **or one of its service providers**; the rule does not require a particular form or make the bank the counterparty.\n\nKeep that regulatory scope separate from the bank’s reviewed U.S. forms: those forms bind only their named parties (typically the AP and the distributor, sometimes with the trust). A form’s narrower party set describes that contractual route; it does not narrow the rule’s permitted counterparties or make every permitted counterparty a party to that form."}}
